Aut and his siblings are not gods. [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs Marchal]] calls them the archetypal parts of a book, and each of them holds a piece of how a story runs.

[[Aut]] is the Writer, who designs the path he thinks the story should take. [[Divinity/The Narrative/Renge|Renge]] is the Fickle Mistress, the things that might happen instead. [[Divinity/The Narrative/Petr|Petr]] is the Threshold a hero crosses. [[Divinity/The Narrative/Insuperlex|Insuperlex]] is the Mountain set in a hero's way, and [[Divinity/The Narrative/Menhir|the Menhir]] is the Heroes themselves.

Aut and Renge are at odds because their domains overlap. Insuperlex and the Menhir clash the same way. To Renge, anything too powerful to be overcome is a balance breaker, and no story she cares about has room for one. The five keep no council and work together only when they must, and no one who leads a real [[Org/index|Org]] is a friend to any of them.
